.TH FSCK.RUNWAY 8 "" "Runway" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
fsck.runway \- check, repair and compact a Runway boot store
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B fsck.runway
[\fB\-a\fR | \fB\-p\fR | \fB\-y\fR | \fB\-n\fR | \fB\-\-repair\fR | \fB\-\-defrag\fR]
[\fB\-f\fR]
[\fB\-k\fR \fIpassphrase\fR]
[\fB\-\-tpm\fR \fIdevice\fR]
[\fB\-\-member\fR \fIstore\fR]...
.I store
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B fsck.runway
checks the structures of a Runway store: both superblocks, the generation in use,
block headers, inodes, extents, the block bitmap, the directory tree, the boot
configuration under
.IR EFI/RUNWAY ,
and the recovery area.
It is the file system checker used by
.BR fsck (8)
for file system type
.BR runway .
.PP
By default it only reads the store.
The repair is conservative.
It fixes leftover blocks that are marked but no longer reachable,
and the boot counter or the state record of the boot configuration.
It publishes one new generation and refuses to touch a store with any other kind of damage.
It does not salvage data.
.PP
A repair or a compaction takes an exclusive lock on the store.
Stop every other writer first (unmount the FUSE daemon, halt EFI sessions).
.PP
An encrypted store is checked in full only with a key.
Without a key, the physical structures and the key slot header are checked,
and a repair or a compaction is refused.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-p ", " \-y ", " \-\-repair
Repair what can be repaired safely, as described above.
The three short options have the same effect, because no repair asks a question.
.TP
.B \-n
Check only and never write.
This is the default.
.TP
.B \-f
Accepted for compatibility with
.BR fsck (8).
The check is always complete.
.TP
.B \-\-defrag
Compact the store offline.
Every object is repacked into one run of blocks, in a single new generation
with the same visible contents.
Nothing is written if the store is already compact.
The store must be free of errors.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " \-\-key " \fIpassphrase\fR"
Passphrase of an encrypted store.
It is visible in the process list;
prefer the environment variable
.BR RWY_KEY .
.TP
.BI \-\-tpm " device"
TPM device used to read the anti-rollback counter of an enrolled store.
The counter is never incremented.
.TP
.BI \-\-member " store"
Another store of the same mirror (may be repeated).
Its recovery area is compared with the one of
.IR store ;
a difference is a warning.
.PP
A mirror health counter in the state record is a warning, one per member.
An orphan content blob in
.I EFI/RUNWAY/BLOBS/
(no slot links it) and a staging file are warnings.
.B \-\-repair
leaves them;
.B rwyctl check \-\-repair \-\-unlock
removes them.
.B rwyctl mirror clear
drops the counters after a repair.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a short usage message and exit with status 16.
.PP
Only one of
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-p ,
.BR \-y ,
.BR \-\-repair ,
.B \-\-defrag
and
.B \-n
may be given.
.SH STORE
.I store
is one of:
.IP \(bu 2
a file or a block device, for example
.IR /dev/sda2 ;
.IP \(bu 2
.BI PARTUUID= uuid\fR;
.IP \(bu 2
.IR image@offset [\fB+\fIlength\fR],
a store inside an image, with the offset and the length in bytes
(decimal or with a
.B 0x
prefix).
.PP
When given a FAT volume or a disk, the checker looks for
.I RUNWAY.DAT
on the ESP.
.SH EXIT STATUS
The exit status follows
.BR fsck (8).
.TP
.B 0
No errors.
A repair that had nothing to do, and a compaction, also exit with 0.
.TP
.B 1
Errors were corrected.
.TP
.B 4
Errors were left uncorrected:
the store is damaged, or a repair or compaction was refused.
A refused fix leaves the store untouched.
.TP
.B 8
Operational error:
the store cannot be opened or locked, the key is wrong, or an I/O error stopped a fix.
After an I/O error the store still has a valid generation, and the fix can be run again.
.TP
.B 16
Usage error.
.PP
The value 2 (reboot needed) is never returned.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RWY_KEY
Passphrase of an encrypted store, if
.B \-k
is not given.
.TP
.B RWY_TPM
TPM device, if
.B \-\-tpm
is not given.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check a store without writing:
.PP
.RS
fsck.runway /dev/disk/by-partuuid/0a1b2c3d\-01
.RE
.PP
Repair an encrypted store, with the key from the environment:
.PP
.RS
RWY_KEY=secret fsck.runway \-a /dev/sda2
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fsck (8),
.BR mount (8),
.BR mount.runway (8),
.BR rwyctl (1),
.BR rwy\-fuse (1)
